WEBVTT

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.390
Sella! Leys!

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.390
Today is Christmas Day!

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.510
How are the preparations
for the party going?

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.390
There are no issues.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:20.820
Everything from the entrance to the corridors
up to the party room is in order.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.940
Preparations in the kitchen are also done.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.950
We will bring in the guests a little later.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.040
And then,

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.160
what about that thingie?

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.410
It is right here!

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:43.050
How tiny!

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.420
Look, Rin!

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.160
The downtown area is so beautiful!

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.410
Sakura, you sure seem thrilled.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:04.350
Well, of course! We're going to spend
Christmas at a castle! How cool is that?

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.340
I can't wait to taste Sella's cooking!

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:11.430
Shirou wanted to help
with the preparations, so he left early.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:16.310
Yes. I am looking forward
to Shirou's cooking, as well.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:21.140
Indeed, with those two cooking,
it can only be awesome.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:27.200
Sakura was so excited about it last night,
she could hardly fall asleep.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:31.570
R-Rider! Don't say things
that'll embarrass me!

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:44.060
The Einzbern Castle is really
in the middle of nowhere, isn't it?

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:47.300
If it were closer,
it'd be so much easier to visit.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.800
Come to think of it, it seems
like it's taking longer than usual to get there.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:55.940
There was more traffic than usual,
so we're running a little late.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:57.810
Let's take a shortcut.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:02:59.810
Shortcut?

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:07.070
This isn't a shortcut!
It's just mountain trails!

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.070
Are we really okay?

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:11.710
We are fine.

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.320
This will get us there in time.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:16.070
That's not the point!

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:25.460
- Nooo!
- Nooo!

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.460
What are we gonna go?
What are we gonna do about this?

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.960
Oops.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:30.590
Allow me!

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.510
Rider?

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.240
I'll get you to safety!

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.520
Please hang on!

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.450
Shirou! Shirou!

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:59.790
Illya, it's not safe,
so don't come close, okay?

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.200
Okay!

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:11.170
Potato pancakes.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.610
You shallow-fry grated potatoes.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.560
It's a German specialty dish.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.390
Don't worry, Sella.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:30.110
Shirou's cooking is really delicious!

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:35.610
I allowed him into the kitchen
because you, Ms. Illya, said so, but...

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.030
Mr. Emiya...

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:42.120
If you should try to serve
something unworthy of her,

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:46.870
I will banish you from the kitchen
immediately! You have been warned!

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.380
Shirou will be fine. Don't worry!

00:04:54.970 --> 00:05:00.600
TIRED

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.850
WE ARE HERE

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:58.140
Sella, here are our guests.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.600
CASTLE?

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.600
SHIROU!

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.580
Thank you.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:04.100
Shirou, have you finished
helping with the preparations?

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:07.480
Nope, I still have
a few things left to do.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.900
Guess it can't be helped.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:12.940
Why don't we all help out?

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:14.490
Okay!

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.250
Merry Christmas!

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.580
How awesome!

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:11.750
The decorations are so beautiful!

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:14.130
What a lovely Christmas!

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:15.470
Magnificent!

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:19.010
I never dreamed
I would see a feast like this!

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:26.350
Indeed, not only is it sumptuous
to the eye, but it's very delicious, too.

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:29.160
The beef is so tender
that it melts in your mouth!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.310
Sella, you're a fabulous cook!

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.060
Yes, but this is delicious, too.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:38.070
Shirou's roast beef.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:41.710
I had Leys and Sella
do most of the cooking,

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:44.380
but Shirou kindly brought
his own dish, too.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.670
I see.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.330
So that big block of meat
got transformed into this!

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.870
A LITTLE EARLIER

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.380
How thick is that?

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:59.590
Normally it'd be too expensive,

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:02.970
but since it's a special occasion,
I decided to splurge.

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:07.100
First, let the meat sit
until it's at room temperature,

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.390
and then salt it generously.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:13.140
Rub the salt and mashed garlic
into the meat well.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.020
Wrap it in plastic wrap,

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:19.150
and let it rest for 15 to 30 minutes,
allowing the flavors to settle.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:23.290
Next, pour some oil into the frying pan,

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.620
and cook the mashed garlic pieces
used to season the meat over low heat

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.660
until it's fragrant.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:30.300
Take out the garlic pieces,

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.920
turn up the heat,
then put the meat in the pan.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:39.130
Cook all four sides, two minutes each,
browning each surface well.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.690
Put the lid on, turn off the heat,

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.100
and let the residual heat
cook it further for five minutes.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:49.650
Turn the meat over, put the lid back on,

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:52.230
and cook on very low heat
for three to four more minutes.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:56.360
Pierce the meat in the center
with a skewer for a few seconds,

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:59.190
then check it by placing it
under your lip.

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:03.320
If the skewer feels warm, that's a sign
that it's been cooked through.

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:08.580
Finally, season the entire block of meat
generously with coarsely ground pepper.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:12.210
Immediately wrap the cooked meat
with plastic wrap and aluminum foil,

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:15.380
and let it rest for about 30 minutes,
and you're done!

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:22.960
Now all you have to do is make gravy
with the juice left in the frying pan.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:27.230
I really wanted to use fillet mignon,
but it was out of my reach.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:30.220
No worries! This is delicious!

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.980
It's so yummy, Shirou!

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:42.540
Mr. Emiya, I have to say,

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.740
Ms. Illya is accustomed to having
cuts of meat of much higher quality.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:49.620
W-Well, I'm sure that's the case.

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:50.740
Sella!

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:54.290
Lower quality or not.

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:57.890
Well, you know, it turned out
to be better than expected.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.250
Shirou, Sella is complimenting you.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.300
L-Leysritt!

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.390
Wasn't that good, Rider?

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:17.730
Yes, very much so.

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:24.230
What's wrong, Rin?

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:27.670
I feel like there's something missing.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:30.240
It must be that thing.

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:32.580
Rin, what do you mean by "that thing"?

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.080
He's back!

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.180
Huh?

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:52.400
I'm totally lost.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.260
Where's the bathroom?

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.710
Oh, was it Leys?

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.280
Maybe she left this
laying out here by mistake.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.710
Here we go.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:36.930
Welcome back, Berserker!

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:38.820
It's huge!

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:42.610
So it was Berserker's job
to bring the tree, huh?

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:45.270
From where?

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:47.990
Now then, Leysritt, let's hurry!

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:48.700
Yes!

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.540
Now it feels a lot more like Christmas.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:03.290
Wait! I have something
for you, Berserker!

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:06.290
Here you go! A Christmas present!

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:13.110
Yes. I know. I know.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:16.050
By the way,
this is the one that Sakura made.

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:19.160
It's an icing cookie.

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:21.560
You're so good at it, Sakura!

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:25.940
We made cookies for you, Berserker.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:27.940
Will you accept them?

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:42.470
Illya, shall we eat
the cookies we baked?

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:46.710
Rin made us apple compote with wine.

00:11:46.710 --> 00:11:49.890
Sakura, we have stollen, too.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.840
Let's all have some dessert!

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:56.340
Oh, Berserker, I forgot to tell you...

00:11:57.060 --> 00:11:59.100
Merry Christmas!
